{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AbbVie Inc. Declares an Increase in the Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on February 14, 2020; Revises Earning Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': "AbbVie Inc. announced that its board of directors declared an increase in the company's quarterly cash dividend from $1.07 per share to $1.18 per share beginning with the dividend payable on February 14, 2020 to shareholders of record as of January 15, 2020. This reflects an increase of approximately 10.3%, continuing the company's strong commitment to returning cash to shareholders through a growing dividend.AbbVie is updating its GAAP diluted EPS guidance for the full-year 2019 from $5.69 to $5.79 to $5.08 to $5.10, representing growth of 39.1% at the midpoint, inclusive of a non-cash charge for SKYRIZI contingent consideration following regulatory approvals in the second quarter and a third-quarter impairment charge related to intangible assets acquired as part of the 2016 acquisition of Stemcentrx Inc."}{'symbol': 'ACN', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Accenture Names John Walsh Group Chief Executive- Communications, Media & Tech', 'text': 'ACCENTURE NAMES JOHN WALSH GROUP CHIEF EXECUTIVE — COMMUNICATIONS, MEDIA & TECHNOLOGY, SUCCEEDING OMAR ABBOSH.'}{'symbol': 'AAP', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Advance Auto Parts Launches Integrated Training Curriculum to Serve the Full Life Cycle of Automotive Technicians', 'text': 'Advance Auto Parts, Inc. has launched a new learning management system designed to provide training programs that grow an automotive professional’s knowledge and skills throughout their entire career. Advance regularly serves more than 26,000 individuals in North America each year with training courses offered through the company’s Carquest Technical Institute (CTI) and Worldpac Training Institute (WTI) programs. Training from Advance now combines courses available online and in the classroom from CTI+WTI into an integrated training solution, giving aftermarket professionals access to a robust library of technical training and business management education. Career Pathways, which feature a structured set of online and classroom events to establish mastery of technical and business competencies, are currently targeted to the General Service Technician and Professional Technician, with Senior Technician, Master Technician, and a number of specialist programs coming by the end of the year. Shop owners can track the progress of their technicians and staff through Career Pathways specific to the type of work they perform at their shop. Training participants receive certifications within the CTI+WTI platform as they complete training programs and advance in their career.'}{'symbol': 'AKAM', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Akamai Technologies, Inc. to Officially Open its New Global Headquarters at 145 Broadway on November 1, 2019', 'text': 'Akamai Technologies, Inc. will officially open its new global headquarters at 145 Broadway on November 1, 2019. The building was developed and is owned by Boston Properties which has granted Akamai a 15-year lease. The architect for the interior work was Watertown-based Sasaki. The general contractor for the interior buildout was the Boston office of Turner Construction.'}{'symbol': 'ALB', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Albemarle Corporation (NYSE:ALB) completed the acquisition of 60% stake in Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine from Mineral Resources Limited (ASX:MIN).', 'text': "Albemarle Corporation (NYSE:ALB) signed an exclusivity agreement to acquire 50% stake in Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine from Mineral Resources Limited (ASX:MIN) for approximately $1.2 billion on November 21, 2018. Albemarle Corporation entered into a binding asset sale and share subscription agreement to acquire 50% stake in Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine from Mineral Resources Limited on December 14, 2018. Albemarle Corporation entered into a revised agreement to acquire 60% stake in Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine from Mineral Resources Limited (ASX:MIN) for approximately $1.3 billion on August 1, 2019. The consideration will be paid in cash upon completion of the acquisition. Albemarle Corporation will fund the acquisition with available cash and new credit facilities. The transaction was funded by borrowing of approximately $900 million under an unsecured credit facility.\n\nUnder the terms of the agreement, Albemarle Corporation and Mineral Resources Limited shall enter into 50/50 fully integrated joint venture and is subject to negotiation of definitive documents and Board approval by the parties. Albemarle Corporation would manage the marketing and sales of lithium hydroxide produced by the joint venture. Albemarle would acquire 50% interest in all mineral rights within the Wodgina tenements, other than iron ore and tantalum, all fixed infrastructure and utility assets, the sodumene concentration plant and the mobile mining equipment. If the agreement are terminated prior to completion, Albemarle will pay a break fee of $100 million to Mineral Resources Limited. The terms as well includes an exclusivity period until December 14, 2018 for the parties to agree upon and execute binding definitive documents. As per the revised agreement, Albemarle Corporation and Mineral Resources Limited shall enter into a 60:40 unincorporated joint venture for operation of the Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine and Kemerton Modules. Under the term of the revised agreement, Albemarle Corporation will pay $820 million in cash upon completion and 40% interest in the first two 25 Ktpa modules of the Kemerton facility.\n\nCompletion of the transaction will be subject to satisfaction of conditions of an administrative nature, applicable regulatory approvals including The Australian Foreign Investment Review Board and any third party consents. As per the revised agreement, the transaction is subject to FIRB approval for the transfer of the Wodgina sale interest, SAMR approval, ministerial consent, third party consent, transfer of the Kemerton sale interest under the Kmerton sale agreement and transfer of Kemerton assets under the Albermarle intra-group transfer. As of July 25, 2019, China State Administration for Market Regulation has approved the transaction. As of October 25, 2019, transaction was approved by FIRB. The transaction will be accretive to Albemarle's earnings. As of December 14, 2018, subject to regulatory approval, completion is expected to take place in second half of 2019. The transaction is expected to complete by December 15, 2019. As of October 28, 2019, completion is expected to occur within the next 10 business days. The transaction will be accretive to Albemarle's earnings. Macquarie Capital (Australia) Limited acted as financial advisor and Gilbert + Tobin acted as legal advisor to Mineral Resources Limited. Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated acted as financial advisor and MinterEllison acted as legal advisor to Albemarle Corporation. Shearman & Sterling LLP acted as legal advisor to Albemarle Corporation.\nAlbemarle Corporation (NYSE:ALB) completed the acquisition of 60% stake in Wodgina Hard Rock Lithium Mine from Mineral Resources Limited (ASX:MIN) on November 1, 2019. The proceed from transaction resulted in Mineral Resources Limited moving to a net cash position and Mineral Resources Limited intends to reinvest or retain the proceeds from the partial sale of Wodgina. \n"}{'symbol': 'AIG', 'date': '2019-11-01 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AIG Reports Qtrly Earnings Per Share Of $0.72', 'text': 'AIG - QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.72; QTRLY ADJUSTED AFTER-TAX EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.56.AIG - QTRLY NET INCOME INCLUDES A PRE-TAX NET REALIZED CAPITAL GAINS OF $929 MILLION.AIG - QTRLY TOTAL GENERAL INSURANCE NET PREMIUMS WRITTEN $6,648 MILLION, DOWN 3%.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.00 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AIG - QTRLY TOTAL GENERAL INSURANCE GROSS PREMIUMS WRITTEN $8,583 MILLION, DOWN 1%.AIG - QTRLY TOTAL GENERAL INSURANCE UNDERWRITING LOSS OF $249 MILLION VERSUS LOSS OF $1,726 MILLION.AIG - AS OF SEPT 30, BOOK VALUE PER COMMON SHARE WAS $74.85 VERSUS $65.04 AT DEC 31, 2018.AIG - QTRLY NET PRE-TAX CATASTROPHE LOSSES OF $511 MILLION VERSUS $1.6 BILLION IN PRIOR-YEAR QUARTER.AIG CEO SAYS Q3 "RESULTS ARE IN LINE WITH OUR EXPECTATIONS, PARTICULARLY IN GENERAL INSURANCE".AIG - "REMAIN CONFIDENT" WILL DELIVER UNDERWRITING PROFITABILITY FOR FY 2019 & DELIVER DOUBLE-DIGIT ROCE BY END OF 2021.AIG - QTRLY ANNUAL ACTUARIAL ASSUMPTION UPDATE CHARGE OF $173 MILLION VERSUS $103 MILLION IN PRIOR-YEAR QUARTER.AIG - LIFE AND RETIREMENT BUSINESS ON TRACK TO DELIVER DOUBLE-DIGIT RETURNS FOR FULL YEAR.'}{'symbol': 'AIG', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American International Group Declares Quarterly Common Stock Cash Dividend, Payable on December 26, 2019; Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend on Series A 5.85% Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock, Payable on December 16, 2019', 'text': 'American International Group, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.32 per share on AIG Common Stock, par value $2.50 per share. The dividend is payable on December 26, 2019 to stockholders of record at the close of business on December 12, 2019.The Board also declared a quarterly cash dividend of $365.625 per share on AIG Series A 5.85% Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock, with a liquidation preference of $25,000 per share, which are represented by depositary shares, each representing a 1/1,000th interest in a share of preferred stock. Holders of depositary shares will receive $0.365625 per depositary share. The dividend is payable on December 16, 2019 to holders of record at the close of business on November 29, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'AMGN', 'date': '2019-11-01 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': "AbbVie Says Doesn't View Any Change In Humira Pricing Going Into 2020", 'text': 'ABBVIE SAYS LAUNCH OF PSORIASIS DRUG SKYRIZI "IS GOING EXTREMELY WELL" AND COMMERCIAL ACCESS FOR THE DRUG IS AT MORE THAN 80% - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SEES "VERY LITTLE CANNIBALIZATION" TO HUMIRA SALES FROM ITS NEW RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS DURG RINVOQ - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SAYS NEW RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS DRUG RINVOQ HAS OUTPACED JOHNSON & JOHNSON\'S REMICADE AND IS CLOSE TO OUTPACING AMGEN\'S ENBREL - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SAYS INTERNATIONAL BIOSIMILAR TRENDS AND DYNAMICS FOR HUMIRA RIVALS REMAIN CONSISTENT WITH EXPECTATIONS - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SEES 2019 REVENUE GROWTH OF 2.5% ON OPERATIONAL BASIS - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE EXPECTS 2019 NON-GAAP TAX RATE JUST BELOW FULL YEAR RATE IN 2018- CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SAYS HAS NOTIFIED FTC OF INTENT TO DIVEST TWO ASSETS FOR ALLERGAN DEAL TO GO THROPUGH - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE SAYS SEEING "SEVERAL INTERESTED PARTIES" FOR ASSETS IT PLANS TO DIVEST FOR ITS ALLERGAN DEAL - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE DOESN\'T VIEW ANY CHANGE IN HUMIRA PRICING GOING INTO 2020- CONF. CALL.ABBVIE CEO SAYS SUPPORTIVE OF SENATE FINANCE COMMITTEE PROPOSAL ON DRUG PRICING "WITH MODIFICATIONS" - CONF. CALL.ABBVIE EXPECTS ALLERGAN\'S BOTOX TO CONTINUE TO PERFORM WELL DESPITE COMPETITION GOING FORWARD, NOTES IT IS DIFFICULT TO DEVELOP A BIOSIMILAR FOR THE PRODUCT - CONF. CALL.'}{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ANSYS, Inc. Announces Resignation of William R. Mcdermott from the Board of Directors', 'text': "On October 28, 2019, William R. McDermott provided ANSYS, Inc. notice of his resignation from the Board of Directors effective October 31, 2019 due to his assumption of the position of President and Chief Executive Officer of ServiceNow, Inc. In connection with Mr. McDermott's resignation, the Board approved the reduction in the size of the Board from eight to seven directors and the number of Class III directors from three to two directors."}{'symbol': 'AMAT', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Applied Materials, Inc., Q4 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 14, 2019', 'text': 'Applied Materials, Inc., Q4 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 14, 2019'}{'symbol': 'ANET', 'date': '2019-11-01 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Arista Networks Posts Q3 Adj EPS Of $2.69', 'text': 'ARISTA NETWORKS, INC. REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.69.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.59.Q3 REVENUE $654.4 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $653.2 MILLION.SEES Q4 2019 REVENUE $540 MILLION TO $560 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.41 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."EXPECT A SUDDEN SOFTENING IN Q4 WITH A SPECIFIC CLOUD TITAN CUSTOMER".ARISTA NETWORKS -SEES Q4 NON-GAAP OPERATING MARGIN OF ABOUT 36%.ARISTA NETWORKS -SEES Q4 NON-GAAP GROSS MARGIN BETWEEN 63% TO 65%.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $686.2 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'AIZ', 'date': '2019-11-01 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Assurant Acquires Global Cell Phone Repair Operator CPR', 'text': 'ASSURANT ACQUIRES GLOBAL CELL PHONE REPAIR OPERATOR CPR.ASSURANT INC - FINANCIAL TERMS OF TRANSACTION WERE NOT DISCLOSED..'}{'symbol': 'T', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'AT&T Inc. Announces Appointment of Stephen Luczo to its Board of Directors and Corporate Development and Finance Committee', 'text': 'AT&T Inc. announced that Stephen Luczo has been elected to the company’s Board of Directors, effective immediately. Mr. Luczo is Chairman of the Board of Seagate Technology and has served in this role since 2002. From October 2017 to October 2018, he also served as Executive Chairman. Before that, he served two tenures as CEO and Chairman. Mr. Luczo’s election brings the number of seats on the AT&T Board of Directors to 14. He will serve on the Board’s Corporate Development and Finance Committee. Stephen Luczo has served as Seagate Technology’s Chairman of the Board since 2002. From October 2017 to October 2018, he also served as Executive Chairman. Before that, he served two tenures as the company’s Chief Executive Officer and Chairman.'}{'symbol': 'ADSK', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Autodesk, Inc., Q3 2020 Earnings Call, Nov 26, 2019', 'text': 'Autodesk, Inc., Q3 2020 Earnings Call, Nov 26, 2019'}{'symbol': 'BLL', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ball Reports Q3 EPS OF 27 Cents', 'text': 'BALL REPORTS IMPROVED THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 REVENUE $2.95 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $3.04 BILLION.Q3 U.S. GAAP EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE OF 27 CENTS.Q3 COMPARABLE EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE OF 70 CENTS.AEROSPACE CONTRACTED BACKLOG INCREASED TO $2.2 BILLION AT QUARTER-END.QTRLY NET SALES $2,953MLN VERSUS $2,946 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.72, REVENUE VIEW $3.04 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'BRK-B', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc. to Report Q3, 2019 Results on Nov 02, 2019', 'text': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc. announced that they will report Q3, 2019 results at 7:00 AM, Central Standard Time on Nov 02, 2019'}{'symbol': 'BIO', 'date': '2019-11-01 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Bio Rad Laboratories Posts Q3 Adj EPS Of $1.61', 'text': 'BIO-RAD REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.61.Q3 SALES ROSE 2.8 PERCENT TO $560.6 MILLION.Q3 LOSS PER SHARE $8.68.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.41, REVENUE VIEW $565.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'BWA', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Borgwarner Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $0.94', 'text': 'BORGWARNER REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 U.S. GAAP NET EARNINGS OF $0.94 PER DILUTED SHARE, OR $0.96 PER DILUTED SHARE EXCLUDING NON-COMPARABLE ITEMS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.96.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.94.Q3 SALES $2.492 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.39 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.85 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NET SALES ARE EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF $9.95 BILLION TO $10.1 BILLION FOR 2019.EXPECTS ITS BLENDED LIGHT-VEHICLE MARKET TO DECLINE IN RANGE OF 4.0% TO 4.5% IN 2019.GLOBAL LIGHT VEHICLE PRODUCTION EXPECTATIONS REMAIN VOLATILE, PARTICULARLY IN CHINA.FOREIGN CURRENCIES ARE EXPECTED TO RESULT IN A YEAR-OVER-YEAR DECREASE IN SALES OF $375 MILLION FOR 2019.ADJUSTED. OPERATING MARGIN IS EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF 11.7% TO 12.0% FOR 2019.ADJUSTED. NET EARNINGS ARE EXPECTED TO BE WITHIN A RANGE OF $3.85 TO $4.00 PER DILUTED SHARE FOR 2019.FULL-YEAR FREE CASH FLOW IS EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF $550 MILLION TO $600 MILLION.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $3.82, REVENUE VIEW $9.99 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'BR', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Broadridge Financial Solutions, Inc. (NYSE:BR) completed the acquisition of Fi360, Inc. for approximately $120 million.', 'text': 'Broadridge Financial Solutions, Inc. (NYSE:BR) entered into an agreement to acquire Fi360, Inc. on October 10, 2019. The transaction is subject to the satisfaction of customary closing conditions, including regulatory approvals, and antitrust approval. As of October 25, 2019, the transaction is approved by Federal Tarde Commission. The transaction is expected to close in November. Raymond James & Associates, Inc. acted as financial advisor to Fi360. Daniel Berick of Squire Patton Boggs (US) LLP acted as legal advisor to Broadridge Financial Solutions, Inc.\nBroadridge Financial Solutions, Inc. (NYSE:BR) completed the acquisition of Fi360, Inc. for approximately $120 million on November 1, 2019. The purchase price is subject to normal closing adjustments.\n'}{'symbol': 'COF', 'date': '2019-11-01 17:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Capital One Says Received Inquiries Relating To Cybersecurity Incident From Some State AGs', 'text': 'CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL SAYS RECEIVED SUBPOENA FROM NEW YORK ATTORNEY GENERAL’S OFFICE IN AUGUST 2019 - SEC FILING.CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL SAYS ALSO RECEIVED SUBPOENA FROM U.S. ATTORNEY’S OFFICE FOR SOUTHERN DISTRICT OF NEW YORK, CIVIL DIVISION, IN OCTOBER 2019.CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL SAYS SUBPOENAS RELATE TO INVESTIGATIONS OF TAXI MEDALLION FINANCE INDUSTRY CO EXITED BEGINNING IN 2015.CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORP - SUBPOENAS SEEK, AMONG OTHER THINGS, INFORMATION REGARDING LENDING COUNTERPARTIES AND PRACTICES - SEC FILING.CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL - RECEIVED INQUIRIES, INFORMATION REQUESTS RELATING TO CYBERSECURITY INCIDENT FROM ABOUT DOZEN STATE ATTORNEYS GENERAL.'}{'symbol': 'CBOE', 'date': '2019-11-01 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cboe Global Markets Reports Results For Third Quarter 2019', 'text': 'CBOE GLOBAL MARKETS REPORTS RESULTS FOR THIRD QUARTER 2019.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.94.Q3 REVENUE ROSE 9 PERCENT TO $294 MILLION.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.29.BOARD INCREASED SHARE REPURCHASE AUTHORIZATION BY $250 MILLION.QTRLY TOTAL COMPANY OPTIONS ADV 7,720 MILLION VERSUS 6,733 MILLION.BOARD INCREASED SHARE REPURCHASE AUTHORIZATION BY $250 MILLION.QTRLY FUTURES ADV 279000 VERSUS 239000.QTRLY OPTIONS NET REVENUE OF $146.5 MILLION, UP  10 PERCENT FROM Q3 OF 2018.QTRLY FUTURES NET REVENUE OF $38.3 MILLION, UP 28 PERCENT.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.15, REVENUE VIEW $290.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CBOE', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'David Howson Announces Executive Changes', 'text': 'Cboe Global Markets, Inc. announced that Mark Hemsley, Executive Vice President at Cboe Global Markets and President of Cboe Europe, is planning to retire from the company at the end of February 2020. David Howson, Chief Operating Officer of Cboe Europe has been named his successor and plans to assume the role of Executive Vice President at Cboe Global Markets and President of Cboe Europe beginning January 1, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'CNC', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Centene Corporation has announced a Fixed-Income Exchange Offer.', 'text': 'Centene Corporation has announced a Fixed-Income Exchange Offer.'}{'symbol': 'CERN', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cerner Corporation Announces Executive Resignations', 'text': 'Cerner Corporation announced that Jeff Townsend, Executive Vice President and Chief of Innovation of Cerner, retired from such role effective November 1, 2019, and transitioned to Executive Senior Advisor. Cerner previously disclosed that it had received notice from Mr. Townsend of his intent to retire by the end of the year. On October 30, 2019, Michael R. Nill, Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer of Cerner Corporation (“Cerner” or the “Company”), announced he will be departing the Company as of the close of business on January 10, 2020, following 23 years at Cerner.'}{'symbol': 'CF', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'CF Industries Holdings, Inc. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-13-2019 10:15 AM', 'text': 'CF Industries Holdings, Inc. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-13-2019 10:15 AM. Venue: Four Seasons Hotel, Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Speakers: Christopher D. Bohn, Senior VP & CFO.'}{'symbol': 'CVX', 'date': '2019-11-01 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Chevron Corp Says Qtrly Adj EPS Of $1.55', 'text': 'CHEVRON CORP - QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.55.CHEVRON CORP SEES FY 2019 PRODUCTION GROWTH (EXCLUDING ASSET SALES) IN MIDDLE OF THE 4-7% RANGE.CHEVRON CORP SEES FY UPSTREAM ASSET SALES PRODUCTION IMPACT (ABOUT 30 MBOED).CHEVRON CORP SEES FY UPSTREAM TCO CO-LENDING OF LESS THAN $2 BILLION.CHEVRON CORP - UPDATES COST ESTIMATE FOR TENGIZ EXPANSION PROJECT TO $45.2 BILLION.CHEVRON ON UPDATE FOR TENGIZ EXPANSION PROJECT, SAYS ITS C&E GUIDANCE IS UNCHANGED FOR 2020 AND 2021 TO 2023 PERIODS.'}{'symbol': 'CVX', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Chevron Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.36', 'text': 'REPORTS THIRD QUARTER NET INCOME OF $2.6 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.36.Q3 SALES $35 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $37.69 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.45 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.WORLDWIDE NET OIL-EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS 3.03 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY IN Q3 2019, AN INCREASE OF 3 PERCENT FROM 2.96 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY FROM A YEAR AGO.CORP - U.S. DOWNSTREAM OPERATIONS EARNED $389 MILLION IN Q3 2019, COMPARED WITH EARNINGS OF $748 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.CORP - U.S. UPSTREAM OPERATIONS EARNED $727 MILLION IN Q3 2019, COMPARED WITH $828 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.CORP - INTERNATIONAL UPSTREAM OPERATIONS EARNED $1.98 BILLION IN Q3 2019, COMPARED WITH $2.55 BILLION A YEAR AGO.CORP - U.S. REFINERY CRUDE OIL INPUT IN Q3 2019 INCREASED 8 PERCENT TO 992,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM YEAR-AGO PERIOD.CORP - INTERNATIONAL DOWNSTREAM OPERATIONS EARNED $439 MILLION IN Q3 2019, COMPARED WITH $625 MILLION A YEAR EARLIER.CORP - U.S. NET OIL-EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION OF 934,000 BARRELS PER DAY IN Q3 2019 WAS UP 103,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM A YEAR EARLIER.CORP - INTERNATIONAL NET OIL-EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION OF 2.10 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY IN Q3 2019 WAS DOWN 26,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM A YEAR EARLIER.CORP - INTERNATIONAL REFINERY CRUDE OIL INPUT OF 625,000 BARRELS PER DAY IN Q3 2019 DECREASED 85,000 BARRELS PER DAY FROM YEAR-AGO PERIOD.CORP - NET CHARGES IN Q3 2019 WERE $952 MILLION, COMPARED WITH NET CHARGES OF $705 MILLION IN YEAR-AGO PERIOD.'}{'symbol': 'CVX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Chevron Corporation Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Chevron Corporation announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 36,116 million compared to USD 43,987 million a year ago. Net income was USD 2,580 million compared to USD 4,047 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.38 compared to USD 2.13 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.36 compared to USD 2.11 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 110,166 million compared to USD 123,987 million a year ago. Net income was USD 9,534 million compared to USD 11,094 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 5.06 compared to USD 5.84 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 5.02 compared to USD 5.79 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'CHD', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Robert D. Leblanc Announces Retirement from the Board of Church & Dwight Co., Inc', 'text': 'On October 30, 2019, Robert D. LeBlanc notified the Board of Directors of Church & Dwight Co., Inc. that he intends to retire from the Board and will, therefore, not stand for reelection as a member of the Board at the Company’s Annual Meeting of Stockholders to be held on April 30, 2020. Mr. LeBlanc will continue to serve on the Board and as Lead Director and as a member of the Audit Committee and the Executive Committee until the end of his term, which will expire at the end of the 2020 Annual Meeting or when his successor has been elected and qualified. The Company gratefully acknowledges Mr. LeBlanc’s more than two decades of dedicated service on its Board. Mr. LeBlanc’s decision not to seek reelection was not the result of any disagreement with the Company.'}{'symbol': 'CI', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cigna’S Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': "CIGNA’S CONTINUED MOMENTUM DRIVES STRONG THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS AND INCREASED REVENUE AND EARNINGS OUTLOOK.TOTAL REVENUES IN Q3 WERE $38.6 BILLION..QTRLY ADJUSTED REVENUES WERE $35.8 BILLION.QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.57.FY OUTLOOK EXCLUDES IMPACT OF ADDITIONAL PRIOR YEAR RESERVE DEVELOPMENT OF MEDICAL COSTS AND POTENTIAL EFFECTS OF FUTURE SHARE REPURCHASE.QTRLY ADJUSTED INCOME FROM OPERATIONS $4.54 PER SHARE.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.54.HEALTH SERVICES' PROJECTED 2020 RETENTION RATE FOR 2019 SELLING SEASON FOR PHARMACY SERVICES IS 97%.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $4.36, REVENUE VIEW $34.20 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ADJUSTED INCOME FROM OPERATIONS IS NOW PROJECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF $6.38 BILLION TO $6.46 BILLION IN 2019, OR $16.80 TO $17.00 PER SHARE.HEALTH SERVICES' ADJUSTED PHARMACY SCRIPTS ARE EXPECTED TO GROW 25 TO 35 MILLION SCRIPTS ORGANICALLY IN 2020.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $16.81 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED INCOME FROM OPERATIONS, PER SHARE   $ 16.80 TO $17.00.SEES 2019 MEDICAL CARE RATIO 80.8% TO 81.2%.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED REVENUE ABOUT  $138,000 MILLION."}{'symbol': 'C', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citigroup Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of CHF 326.5275 million.', 'text': 'Citigroup Inc. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of CHF 326.5275 million.\n\nSecurity Name: 0.5% Notes due November 01, 2028\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: CHF 325 million\nPrice\\Range: 100.47%\nSecurity Features: Euro MTN; MTN\nCoupon Type: Fixed\n'}{'symbol': 'C', 'date': '2019-11-01 07:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citi names new ESG Chief for markets & securities business', 'text': 'APPOINTS ELREE WINNETT SEELIG TO NEWLY CREATED ROLE OF HEAD OF ESG FOR MARKETS AND SECURITIES SERVICES, REFLECTING GROWING IMPORTANCE OF ESG FOR INDUSTRY AND CLIENTS.'}{'symbol': 'CTXS', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citrix Systems and Aston Martin Red Bull Racing Renew Partnership', 'text': 'CITRIX SYSTEMS INC -  ASTON MARTIN RED BULL RACING AND CITRIX RENEW PARTNERSHIP.'}{'symbol': 'CTXS', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aston Martin Red Bull Racing and Citrix Renews Partnership', 'text': 'Citrix Systems, Inc. and Aston Martin Red Bull Racing announced a renewal of their innovation partnership. A multi-year extension will see Citrix branding remain prominent on and off the Aston Martin Red Bull Racing car, while the Team will rely on Citrix’s innovative digital workspace solutions as it adapts to Formula One’s new technical and regulatory framework. Citrix has been a technical partner of the Team since 2007, delivering digital workspace solutions that allow the race team on the road to access the full processing power of the organization at base. With Citrix technology, Aston Martin Red Bull Racing can access high-powered computing resources from anywhere in the world. This flexibility has proved vital in delivering the Team’s successes. A modern F1 team is a distributed and collaborative network that places an incredibly high value on speed and responsiveness. Against the backdrop of an expanding global racing series, Citrix enables Aston Martin Red Bull Racing to maximize its resources, wherever in the world team members are working.'}{'symbol': 'CLX', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Clorox Reports Q1 Earnings Per Share $1.59', 'text': 'CLOROX REPORTS Q1 FISCAL YEAR 2020 RESULTS, CONFIRMS SALES AND EPS OUTLOOK.REAFFIRMS FY 2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.05 TO $6.25.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.59.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.54 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FIRST-QUARTER RESULTS WERE GENERALLY IN LINE WITH OUR EXPECTATIONS.REMAIN ON TRACK TO DELIVER OUR FISCAL YEAR OUTLOOK.QTRLY NET SALES $1.51 BILLION VERSUS $1.56 BILLION.QTRLY DILUTED EPS RESULTS WERE DUE PRIMARILY TO HIGHER TRADE PROMOTION SPENDING.'}{'symbol': 'CL', 'date': '2019-11-01 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Colgate Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $0.67', 'text': 'COLGATE ANNOUNCES 3RD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.67.Q3 SALES $3.928 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $3.94 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.70 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.71 EXCLUDING ITEMS.NORTH AMERICA NET SALES INCREASED 1.5% IN THIRD QUARTER 2019.QTRLY ORGANIC SALES INCREASED 4.5%.LATIN AMERICA NET SALES INCREASED 3.0% IN Q3 2019.CONTINUE TO EXPECT 2019 NET SALES TO BE FLAT TO UP LOW-SINGLE-DIGITS.COLGATE-PALMOLIVE - DECREASE IN QTRLY NORTH AMERICA GROSS PROFIT PRIMARILY DUE TO HIGHER RAW AND PACKAGING MATERIAL COSTS, PARTIALLY OFFSET BY COST SAVINGS.SEES 2019 ORGANIC SALES NOW EXPECTED TO BE UP BETWEEN 3% AND 4%.NOW EXPECT A SLIGHT DECLINE IN GROSS MARGIN IN 2019.CONTINUE TO PLAN FOR INCREASED ADVERTISING INVESTMENT AND A MID-SINGLE-DIGIT DECLINE IN EARNINGS PER SHARE IN 2019.NET INCOME IN Q3 2019 INCLUDED $36 MILLION ($0.04 PER DILUTED SHARE) OF AFTERTAX CHARGES.FY2019 REVENUE VIEW $15.61 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CL', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Colgate-Palmolive Company Provides Earnings Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': 'Colgate-Palmolive Company provided earnings guidance for the year 2019. For the period, the company expects 2019 net sales to be flat to up low-single-digits, with organic sales now expected to be up between 3% and 4%, roughly in line with year-to-date growth. On a GAAP basis, based on current spot rates, the company now expects a slight decline in gross margin and continue to expect a low-single-digit decline in earnings per share in 2019.'}{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Corteva, Inc. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-12-2019 08:45 AM', 'text': 'Corteva, Inc. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-12-2019 08:45 AM. Venue: Four Seasons Hotel, Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Speakers: James C. Collins, CEO & Director.'}{'symbol': 'DAL', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc. Extends Lakers Partnership', 'text': "Delta Air Lines and the Los Angeles Lakers have agreed to a long-term partnership extension, solidifying Delta's status as the team's official and exclusive airline partner. The new partnership will provide the following core benefits: Delta retains its position as the Lakers' official airline with category exclusivity; An increased presence on Lakers social and digital channels, via unique and innovative programs such as the Showtime Seat Exchange; The customization of courtside seatbacks, to be changed throughout the season, showcasing Delta brand initiatives; Continuation of monthly Salute to Troops programming, which honors U.S. Military living and stationed in Southern California by recognizing them during games and providing honorees tickets to that night's game, a custom Lakers jersey, a challenge coin and the opportunity to attend practice to meet Lakers players and coaches."}{'symbol': 'D', 'date': '2019-11-01 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dominion Energy Q3 Earnings Per Share Estimate $1.14 -- Refinitiv Ibes Data', 'text': 'DOMINION ENERGY ANNOUNCES THIRD-QUARTER EARNINGS.Q3 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.18.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.14 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q4 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.10 TO $1.25.SEES FY 2019 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.15 TO $4.30.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.17.COMPANY NARROWS 2019 OPERATING EARNINGS GUIDANCE.QTRLY OPERATING REVENUE $4,269 MILLION VERSUS $3,451 MILLION.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $4.19 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $4.51 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'D', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dominion Energy, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Dominion Energy, Inc. provides earnings guidance for fourth quarter of 2019. For the period, the company expects operating earnings in the range of $1.10 to $1.25 per share, compared to fourth-quarter 2018 operating earnings of $0.89 per share.'}{'symbol': 'DOW', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ALTIVIA Ketones & Additives, LLC completed the acquisition of Acetone Derivatives Business from Dow Inc.', 'text': 'ALTIVIA Ketones & Additives, LLC entered into an agreement to acquire Acetone Derivatives Business from Dow Inc. (NYSE:DOW) on August 13, 2019. The acquisition includes production assets located in Institute, West Virginia, in addition to the site infrastructure, land and utilities. Dow will remain a tenant on the Institute site, retaining ownership of certain manufacturing assets. The transaction is expected to close by the end of 2019, subject to customary closing conditions.\nALTIVIA Ketones & Additives, LLC completed the acquisition of Acetone Derivatives Business from Dow Inc. (NYSE:DOW) on November 1, 2019. \n'}{'symbol': 'DTE', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'DTE Energy Company Names Joann Chávez as Senior Vice President and Chief Legal Officer', 'text': 'DTE Energy announced JoAnn Chávez will take on the role of senior vice president and chief legal officer. In this expanded role, Chávez will have overall responsibility for the Office of the General Counsel, Ethics & Compliance and Corporate Security.'}{'symbol': 'EFX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Equifax Inc. Announces New Senior Leader for Global Consumer Business', 'text': 'Equifax Inc. has named Beverly Anderson president of Global Consumer Services (GCS), replacing Dann Adams who has announced his retirement. Anderson, an established financial services leader, is joining Equifax from Wells Fargo where she served as Executive Vice President, Cards and Retail Services. For the past seven and a half years, she has been responsible for leading growth and transformation of various lines of lending businesses and operations. Most recently, she led the expansion of the consumer general-purpose credit card, co-brand, private label, and enterprise loyalty businesses.'}{'symbol': 'EQIX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Equinix, Inc. (REIT) Presents at REITworld: 2019 Annual Conference, Nov-12-2019', 'text': 'Equinix, Inc. (REIT) Presents at REITworld: 2019 Annual Conference, Nov-12-2019 . Venue: JW Marriott Los Angeles L.A. Live, 900 West Olymipic Boulevard, Los Angeles, California, United States. Speakers: Charles J. Meyers, President, CEO & Director, Katrina Rymill, Vice President of Investor Relations.'}{'symbol': 'EL', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Estée Lauder Increases Quarterly Dividend 12% To $0.48 Per Share', 'text': 'THE ESTÉE LAUDER COMPANIES INC.INCREASES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND 12% TO $.48 PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'EXC', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Exelon Corporation Declares Regular Quarterly Dividend, Payable on Dec. 10, 2019', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Exelon Corporation declared a regular quarterly dividend of $0.3625 per share on Exelon’s common stock. The dividend is payable on Dec. 10, 2019, to shareholders of record of Exelon as of 5 p.m. Eastern time on Nov. 15, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'EXC', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Exelon Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $0.79', 'text': 'EXELON REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.92.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.79.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.89 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NARROWING GUIDANCE RANGE FOR FULL YEAR 2019 ADJUSTED (NON-GAAP) OPERATING EARNINGS FROM $3.00- $3.30 PER SHARE TO $3.05 - $3.20 PER SHARE.ANNOUNCING ADDITIONAL ANNUAL COST SAVINGS OF $100 MILLION; SAVINGS OF $75 MILLION OF OPERATING AND MAINTENANCE EXPENSES.ANNOUNCING ADDITIONAL ANNUAL COST SAVINGS OF $100 MILLION.ON TRACK TO INVEST MORE THAN $5.4 BILLION AT OUR ELECTRIC AND GAS COMPANIES BY YEAR END.QTRLY OPERATING REVENUES $8,929 MILLION VERSUS $9,403 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'XOM', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation Announces Operating Results for the Third Quarter and Nine Months Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation announced operating results for the third quarter and nine months ended September 30, 2019. For the quarter, the company reported net production of crude oil, natural gas liquids, bitumen and synthetic oil of 2,392,000 barrels per day against 2,286,000 barrels per day a year ago. Oil equivalent production was 3,899 koebd against 3,786 koebd a year ago.For the nine months, the company reported net production of crude oil, natural gas liquids, bitumen and synthetic oil of 2,369,000 barrels per day against 2,238,000 barrels per day a year ago. Oil equivalent production was 3,909 koebd against 3,774 koebd a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'FIS', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'FIS to Build New World Headquarters in Jacksonville, Florida', 'text': 'FIS announced that it has received city and state approvals on an economic development package for plans to build a new, expanded world headquarters in Jacksonville, Florida to support the company’s continued growth. FIS has also entered into a real estate purchase agreement with Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Florida, Inc. (Florida Blue) to purchase the riverfront property located at 323 Riverside Avenue on which to build its headquarters. The agreement is subject to customary diligence and standard contractual closing conditions and is expected to close no later than the second quarter of 2020. FIS will consolidate its current 601 Riverside Avenue headquarters as well as two additional Jacksonville-based facilities into the new headquarters building. The new headquarters building is expected to be 12 stories with approximately 300,000 square feet of space. FIS expects construction on the new headquarters to begin immediately after the closing and to take about two years to complete.'}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ford Motor Co. Plans to Close the Romeo Engine Plant', 'text': 'Ford Motor Co. plans to close the Romeo Engine Plant and relocate or buy out an estimated 600 UAW workers. Plant officials delivered the news to workers during early shifts less than 12 hours after a proposed tentative contract agreement was announced publicly, following three days of intense negotiation.'}{'symbol': 'FTNT', 'date': '2019-11-01 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fortinet Posts Q3 Adj. EPS Of $0.67', 'text': 'FORTINET REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.67.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.46.Q3 REVENUE $547.5 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $532.5 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.56 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q4 2019 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.69 TO $0.71.SEES FY 2019 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.39 TO $2.41.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE $2.135 BILLION TO $2.15 BILLION.SEES Q4 2019 REVENUE $595 MILLION TO $610 MILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.64, REVENUE VIEW $584.8 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.24, REVENUE VIEW $2.11 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY BILLINGS OF $626.6 MILLION, UP 19% YEAR OVER YEAR.QTRLY DEFERRED REVENUE OF $1.95 BILLION, UP 26%.SEES 2019 BILLINGS IN RANGE OF $2.550 BILLION TO $2.565 BILLION.SEES FY NON-GAAP GROSS MARGIN IN RANGE OF 76.5% TO 77.0%.SEES FY NON-GAAP OPERATING MARGIN IN RANGE OF 24.0% TO 24.5%.'}{'symbol': 'IT', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gartner Reports Third Quarter 2019 Financial Results', 'text': 'GARTNER REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.39 TO $3.64.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.09 TO $2.34.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE $4.22 BILLION TO $4.26 BILLION.Q3 REVENUE $1.0 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $991.6 MILLION.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.70.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.46.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.43 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $3.53, REVENUE VIEW $4.24 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'GNRC', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Generac Reports Record Quarterly Results', 'text': 'GENERAC REPORTS RECORD QUARTERLY RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.18.Q3 SALES $601.1 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $582.8 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.33 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.43.GENERAC HOLDINGS - COMPANY IS INCREASING ITS FULL-YEAR 2019 GUIDANCE FOR REVENUE GROWTH.GENERAC HOLDINGS - RAISING FULL-YEAR NET SALES GROWTH TO ABOUT 8 TO 9%, WITH CORE SALES GROWTH EXPECTED TO BE ABOUT 7% VERSUS PRIOR YEAR.GENERAC HOLDINGS - NET INCOME MARGIN, BEFORE DEDUCTING FOR NONCONTROLLING INTERESTS, NOW EXPECTED TO BE ABOUT 11.5% FOR FULL-YEAR 2019.GENERAC HOLDINGS - CONVERSION OF ADJUSTED NET INCOME TO FREE CASH FLOW EXPECTED TO BE ABOUT 80% FOR FY 2019.GENERAC HOLDINGS - OPERATING AND FREE CASH FLOW GENERATION FOR THE FULL YEAR IS STILL EXPECTED TO BE STRONG FOR FY 2019.'}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sangamo Therapeutics Appoints Executive Vice President And Chief Financial Officer', 'text': 'SANGAMO THERAPEUTICS APPOINTS SUNG LEE AS EXECUTIVE VICE PRESIDENT AND CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER.SANGAMO THERAPEUTICS INC - LEE JOINS SANGAMO FROM GILEAD SCIENCES.'}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gilead and Galapagos to Present New Data on Filgotinib At 2019 Acr/Arp Annual Meeting', 'text': "Gilead Sciences, Inc. and Galapagos NV announced that new data from across the companies' inflammatory disease research and development program will be presented at the 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Association of Rheumatology Professionals (ACR/ARP) Annual Meeting in Atlanta from November 8-13. The companies will present 20 abstracts at this year's meeting, including key data on the investigational medicine filgotinib in rheumatoid arthritis (RA) and psoriatic arthritis (PsA), as well as real-world RA treatment outcomes and care. Key presentations include multiple subgroup analyses from the FINCH 2 clinical trial that demonstrate the potential of filgotinib across specific RA populations who have experienced an inadequate response to biologic disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (bDMARDs), including those in this difficult-to-treat population with anemia, thrombocytopenia and leukopenia. Key data will also include pooled safety results from the Phase 3 FINCH program (NCT02889796, NCT02873936, NCT02886728), and safety outcomes from the long-term DARWIN-3 trial (NCT02065700). A Subgroup Analysis of the Efficacy of Filgotinib in Demographic and Clinical Subgroups of Patients with Refractory Rheumatoid Arthritis (Poster, #504, Sunday, Nov. 10; 9:00am) A Subgroup Analysis of Clinical Efficacy Response and Quality of Life Outcomes from Phase 3 Study of Filgotinib in Patients with Inadequate Response to Biologic DMARDs (Poster, #517, Sunday, Nov. 10; 9:00am). In RA, biomarker research seeks to better characterize the molecular basis of the disease and identify populations that may benefit most from a treatment. Gilead is committed to helping drive forward this emerging area of innovation. Presented data will assess the relationship between a series of RA biomarkers and the therapeutic response of filgotinib."}{'symbol': 'GS', 'date': '2019-11-01 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cantor Fitzgerald & Co. Hires Paul Mutter As Head Of Institutional Client Coverage', 'text': 'CANTOR FITZGERALD - MUTTER MOST RECENTLY SERVED AS A MANAGING DIRECTOR AT GOLDMAN SACHS IN THEIR CLIENT RELATIONSHIP MANAGEMENT & STRATEGY DEPARTMENT .CANTOR FITZGERALD & CO. HIRES PAUL MUTTER AS HEAD OF INSTITUTIONAL CLIENT COVERAGE.'}{'symbol': 'IDXX', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Idexx Laboratories Posts Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.24', 'text': 'IDEXX LABORATORIES ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.72 TO $4.78.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.24.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE UP 8 TO 8.5 PERCENT.SEES Q3 2019 REVENUE $605 MILLION.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE $2.395 BILLION TO $2.405 BILLION.SEES Q3 2019 REVENUE UP 11 PERCENT.Q3 REVENUE $605 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $597.1 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.14 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.PRELIMINARY 2020 FINANCIAL GUIDANCE FOR REVENUE GROWTH OF 9% - 10.5% ON A REPORTED AND ORGANIC BASIS.PRELIMINARY 2020 FINANCIAL GUIDANCE FOR EPS OF $5.30 - $5.46.ADJUSTS 2019 EPS OUTLOOK RANGE TO $4.72 - $4.78.2019 EPS OUTLOOK TO $4.72 - $4.78 PER SHARE.SEES FY 2019 CAPITAL EXPENDITURES ABOUT $160 MILLION - $175 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'IP', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'International Paper Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $0.87', 'text': 'INTERNATIONAL PAPER REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.09.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.87.QTRLY NET SALES $5,568 MILLION VERSUS $5,901 MILLION.INDUSTRIAL PACKAGING OPERATING PROFITS IN Q3 OF 2019 WERE $510 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $5.60 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.PRINTING PAPERS OPERATING PROFITS IN Q3 OF 2019 WERE $148 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'IVZ', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Invesco Ltd. Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-06-2019 08:50 AM', 'text': 'Invesco Ltd. Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-06-2019 08:50 AM. Venue: The St. Regis Hotel, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Loren Michael Starr, Senior MD & CFO, Peter Mintzberg, Global Head of Corporate Strategy, Investor Relations & Treasury.'}{'symbol': 'IRM', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Iron Mountain Inc - On Oct. 29 Co Commenced A Global Program Called Project Summit', 'text': 'IRON MOUNTAIN INC - ON OCTOBER 29 CO COMMENCED A GLOBAL PROGRAM CALLED PROJECT SUMMIT.IRON MOUNTAIN - AS A RESULT OF PROGRAM, EXPECT TO REDUCE NUMBER OF VICE PRESIDENT LEVEL AND ABOVE POSITIONS BY ABOUT 45%.IRON MOUNTAIN - TOTAL PROGRAM IS EXPECTED TO REDUCE TOTAL MANAGERIAL AND ADMINISTRATIVE WORKFORCE BY ABOUT 700 POSITIONS OVER NEXT TWO YEARS.IRON MOUNTAIN INC - EXPECT PROJECT SUMMIT TO IMPROVE ADJUSTED EBITDA BY APPROXIMATELY $80.0 MILLION IN 2020.IRON MOUNTAIN INC - ESTIMATE THAT IMPLEMENTATION OF PROJECT SUMMIT WILL RESULT IN TOTAL RESTRUCTURING CHARGES OF APPROXIMATELY $240.0 MILLION.IRON MOUNTAIN INC - ACTIVITIES ASSOCIATED WITH PROJECT SUMMIT WILL BEGIN IN Q4 OF 2019 AND ARE EXPECTED TO BE SUBSTANTIALLY COMPLETE BY END OF 2021.'}{'symbol': 'JPM', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'JPMorgan Chase & Co. Presents at FIMA Europe 2019, Nov-19-2019 through Nov-20-2019', 'text': 'JPMorgan Chase & Co. Presents at FIMA Europe 2019, Nov-19-2019 through Nov-20-2019. Venue: QEII CENTRE, London, United Kingdom. Presentation Date & Speakers: Nov-20-2019, Robin Doyle, Managing Director, Office of Regulatory Affairs.'}{'symbol': 'KEYS', 'date': '2019-11-01 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Keysight Technologies CEO Appointed Chairman Of The Board Of Directors', 'text': "KEYSIGHT TECHNOLOGIES CEO, RON NERSESIAN, APPOINTED CHAIRMAN OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS.KEYSIGHT TECHNOLOGIES INC - RON NERSESIAN, PRESIDENT AND CEO, HAS BEEN APPOINTED CHAIRMAN OF COMPANY'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS, EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY."}{'symbol': 'KEYS', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Keysight Technologies, Inc. Announces Management Changes', 'text': 'Keysight Technologies, Inc. announced that Ron Nersesian, president and chief executive officer, has been appointed chairman of the company’s Board of Directors, effective immediately. Nersesian has served as president and chief executive officer since Keysight launched as an independent public company in 2014 after being spun out of Agilent Technologies. Under Nersesian, Keysight has created strong value for shareholders, customers and employees. With Nersesian’s appointment, Clark will assume the role of lead independent director. As lead independent director, Clark’s responsibilities will include setting the agenda for Board of Directors meetings with Nersesian, liaising between the chairman and independent directors, presiding over meetings of independent directors, and advising on shareholder engagement and governance.'}{'symbol': 'LYB', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'LyondellBasell Industries N.V. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-13-2019 11:00 AM', 'text': 'LyondellBasell Industries N.V. Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-13-2019 11:00 AM. Venue: Four Seasons Hotel, Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Speakers: James Guilfoyle, Executive Vice President, Advanced Polymer Solutions & Global Supply Chain.'}{'symbol': 'MPC', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marathon To Seek Strategic Alternatives', 'text': 'Marathon Petroleum Corporation (NYSE:MPC) Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Gary R. Heminger said, "Today we announced our next step to unlocking future value: our intent to separate Speedway into an independent company. Additionally, we are forming a special committee of the Board of Directors to continue evaluating alternatives to enhance value across our midstream business".'}{'symbol': 'MPC', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marathon Petroleum To Spin-Off Speedway Into An Independent, Publicly Traded Co', 'text': "MARATHON PETROLEUM PROVIDES UPDATE ON STRATEGIC REVIEW TO ENHANCE SHAREHOLDER VALUE.MARATHON PETROLEUM CORP - TO SPIN-OFF SPEEDWAY INTO AN INDEPENDENT, PUBLICLY TRADED COMPANY.MARATHON PETROLEUM CORP - FORMS SPECIAL COMMITTEE OF BOARD OF DIRECTORS TO ENHANCE MIDSTREAM REVIEW.MARATHON PETROLEUM CORP - INDEPENDENT DIRECTOR JOHN P. SURMA WILL LEAD A COMMITTEE OF BOARD TO OVERSEE SEPARATION AND CEO SEARCH PROCESSES..MARATHON PETROLEUM CORP - WILL RETAIN ITS DIRECT-DEALER BUSINESS.MARATHON PETROLEUM CORP - WILL ALSO INITIATE A NATIONWIDE SEARCH FOR A SPEEDWAY CEO FROM BOTH INTERNAL AND EXTERNAL SOURCES.MARATHON PETROLEUM - INDEPENDENT DIRECTOR J. MIKE STICE WILL LEAD SPECIAL COMMITTEE CHARGED WITH THIS ENHANCED EVALUATION OF MIDSTREAM ALTERNATIVES.MARATHON PETROLEUM - INDEPENDENT SPEEDWAY WILL CONSIST OF MPC'S COMPANY-OWNED RETAIL STORE OPERATIONS WITH AN EXPECTED 2019 EBITDA OF ABOUT $1.5 BILLION.MARATHON PETROLEUM - ALTHOUGH SEPARATION OF SPEEDWAY WILL NOT REQUIRE A SHAREHOLDER VOTE, SEPARATION WILL BE SUBJECT TO FINAL APPROVAL BY CO'S BOARD."}{'symbol': 'MKTX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'MarketAxess Holdings Inc. (NasdaqGS:MKTX) completed the acquisition of LiquidityEdge LLC.', 'text': "MarketAxess Holdings Inc. (NasdaqGS:MKTX) entered into an agreement to acquire LiquidityEdge LLC for approximately $150 million on August 12, 2019. The consideration consists of $100 million in cash and $50 million in MarketAxess stock, subject to customary purchase price adjustments. Under the agreement, the sellers are prohibited from transferring any of MarketAxess common stock received in the transaction for a period of six months following the closing, and a portion of the stock consideration will be placed into escrow to secure the sellers’ indemnification obligations under the agreement. LiquidityEdge had a revenue of $9.2 million in 2018. The transaction is subject to the satisfaction of customary closing conditions, Execution of Escrow Agreement, receipt of required antitrust and regulatory approvals including under the HSR Act and from the U.K. Financial Conduct Authority and FINRA, the receipt of certain third-party contractual consents and termination of or entry into certain other contractual arrangements and the absence of any law or governmental order prohibiting the consummation of the transaction. As on August 30, 2019 federal trade commission gave approval for the transaction. The transaction is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2019. Michael J. Aiello of Weil, Gotshal & Manges LLP acted as legal advisor to MarketAxess Holdings Inc. (NasdaqGS:MKTX). James M. Fischer and Beth Diffley of Drinker Biddle & Reath LLP acted as legal advisors to LiquidityEdge LLC.\nMarketAxess Holdings Inc. (NasdaqGS:MKTX) completed the acquisition of LiquidityEdge LLC on November 1, 2019. The purchase price includes $100 million in cash and 146,450 shares of MarketAxess's common stock, subject to customary purchase price adjustments. The following acquisition was completed approval following from the necessary regulatory authorities.\n"}{'symbol': 'MXIM', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Maxim Integrated Products, Inc. Announces New Products in Essential Analog Portfolio in Power, Solution Size and Accuracy', 'text': 'Designers can further reduce power consumption and solution size, while improving measurement accuracy, with three new analog products from Maxim Integrated Products, Inc. The MAX6078A voltage reference IC, the MAX16155 nanoPower supervisor and the MAX16160 voltage monitor and reset IC achieve best-in-class performance for cloud infrastructure, IoT, intelligence-at-the-edge, on-device AI, as well as smart and emerging applications in consumer, communications, industrial and medical markets. As designers develop new and next-generation systems for greater performance, smaller size and innovative capabilities, they demand reliable analog solutions to provide essential performance functions such as precision measurement and reliable protection. Maxim leverages world-class circuit design expertise and unique advanced process technology to provide high-quality building block ICs that support system advances in multiple applications. Maxim has added three new solutions to its Essential Analog portfolio of high-performance, single-function analog ICs which provide efficient power, precision measurement, rugged connectivity and reliable protection. Maxim\'s New Solutions in Essential Analog Portfolio: MAX6078A: Precision Voltage Reference Delivers Industrial Level Accuracy on a Tight Battery Power Budget The MAX6078A features ±0.04%initial accuracy, 20%more accurate than similar competitive devices. At 15µA quiescent current, the MAX6078A opens the potential for precision measurements on battery-powered and energy-harvesting systems. It operates at 6.6x less current than the closest competitive parts and, at 1.458mm x 1.288mm, is 58%smaller than competing solutions. MAX16155: Industry\'s Lowest Power nanoPower Supervisor The MAX16155 consumes just 400nA typical, or only 4% of the supply current that competitive solutions require, providing reliable system protection for virtually no power. It ensures portable, low-power devices operate safely in the event of a power failure or code error by monitoring a system rail for undervoltage fault and keeping the system in reset when it senses the fault along with a watchdog timer. The IC comes in a tiny, 6-pin SOT23 package. MAX16160: New 4-Channel Voltage Monitor and Reset IC Without VCC Rail Power-Up Requirement The MAX16160 is the only 4-channel voltage monitor and reset IC that uniquely asserts reset low without requiring VCC rail if any of the rails is above 1V. It features the industry\'s most reliable start-up and continuous operation of multi-supply systems by asserting output low. This "no-power power-up" eliminates unknown system states and significantly reduces the burden on design engineers to accurately sequence their power rail startup. With a voltage monitoring accuracy of ±1% for all inputs, it is up to 50% more accurate than competitive offerings (commonly ±1.50% for all inputs). Its 6-bump WLP (1.408mm x 0.848mm) is 85% smaller than the closest competitor.'}{'symbol': 'MCO', 'date': '2019-11-01 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Moody's Says The Outlook For U.S. Retail Has Been Revised To Stable From Positive", 'text': "MOODY'S SAYS THE OUTLOOK FOR U.S. RETAIL HAS BEEN REVISED TO STABLE FROM POSITIVE.MOODY'S SAYS LARGE U.S. RETAIL CONTRIBUTORS NEGATIVELY IMPACTED THIS YEAR BY REIMBURSEMENT PRESSURES, SOFTER HOUSING MARKET.MOODY'S-PERFORMANCE ACROSS U.S. RETAIL INDUSTRY FACES RISING PRESSURE, MARKET SHARE COMPETITION, E-COMMERCE INTEGRATION COSTS, BRICK & MORTAR CHANNELS.MOODY'S SAYS U.S. RETAIL WILL CONTINUE TO REAP REWARDS OF STRATEGIC INVESTMENTS IN E-COMMERCE AND IMPROVED OPERATING EFFICIENCIES."}{'symbol': 'MS', 'date': '2019-11-01 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Members Exchange Files Form 1 Application And Exhibits - U.S. SEC', 'text': 'MEMX, LLC FILES FORM 1 APPLICATION AND EXHIBITS - U.S. SEC.MEMX LLC FILES FORM 1 APPLICATION FOR REGISTRATION AS A NATIONAL SECURITIES EXCHANGE - U.S. SEC.'}{'symbol': 'MOS', 'date': '2019-11-01 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Mosaic Company Announced Senior Leadership Changes', 'text': 'THE MOSAIC COMPANY ANNOUNCED SENIOR LEADERSHIP CHANGES.MOSAIC CO - RICK MCLELLAN WILL RETURN TO UNITED STATES TO LEAD COMMERCIAL ORGANIZATION.'}{'symbol': 'MOS', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Mosaic Company Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-12-2019 09:30 AM', 'text': 'The Mosaic Company Presents at Morgan Stanley Global Chemicals and Agriculture Conference, Nov-12-2019 09:30 AM. Venue: Four Seasons Hotel, Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Speakers: Clint C. Freeland, Senior VP & CFO.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-11-01 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Equity trading in Copenhagen, Helsinki and Iceland to start at 1605 CET -Nasdaq', 'text': 'NASDAQ SAYS TRADING IN COPENHAGEN, HELSINKI AND ICELANDIC MARKETS WILL START WITH AN OPENING AUCTION AT 1605 CET FOLLOWED BY AN UNCROSS AT 1615 CET.NASDAQ SAYS THESE MARKETS WILL CLOSE ACCORDING TO THEIR REGULAR SCHEDULE.NASDAQ SAYS EXISTING ORDERS HAVE BEEN FLUSHED.NASDAQ SAYS NASDAQ NORDIC FINNISH AND DANISH EQUITY DERIVATIVES MARKETS WILL OPEN AND THE MARKETS WILL FOLLOW THE BELOW OPENING PROCEDURE: ORDER MANAGEMENT IS VALID FROM CET 1555..NASDAQ SAYS ORDER MANAGEMENT IS VALID FROM CET 1555. TRADING WILL START AT CET 1615. EXISTING ORDERS WILL NOT BE CANCELLED AUTOMATICALLY.NASDAQ SAYS THESE MARKETS WILL ALSO CLOSE ACCORDING TO REGULAR SCHEDULE.NASDAQ SAYS NASDAQ NORDIC INDEX-, EQUITY: SWEDEN WILL REMAIN CLOSED.'}{'symbol': 'NWL', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Newell Brands Inc. Reports Impairment of Goodwill, Intangibles and Other Assets for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019; Revises Earnings Guidance for the Full Year 2019 and Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Newell Brands Inc. revised earnings guidance for the full year 2019 and provides earnings guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. For the year, the company now expects to report net sales in the range of $9.6 billion to $9.7 billion, compared with previous guidance of net sales in the range of $9.1 billion to $9.3 billion. Core sales expected to be low single digit decline.For the fourth quarter of 2019, the company expects to report net sales in the range of $2.5 billion to $2.6 billion, and core sales 2% to 4% decline. For the third quarter ended September 30, 2019, the company reported impairment of goodwill, intangibles and other assets was $834.9 million compared to $8,133.7 million a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'NI', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Nisource Files For Potential Mixed Shelf Offering- SEC Filing', 'text': 'NISOURCE INC FILES FOR POTENTIAL MIXED SHELF OFFERING; SIZE NOT DISCLOSED - SEC FILING.'}{'symbol': 'NI', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'NiSource Inc. has filed a Follow-on Equity Offering in the amount of $434.379942 million.', 'text': 'NiSource Inc. has filed a Follow-on Equity Offering in the amount of $434.379942 million.'}{'symbol': 'NXPI', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'NXP Semiconductors Increases Performance and Expands LPC5500 Arm Cortex-M33 Microcontroller Series', 'text': 'NXP Semiconductors announced the availability of its LPC552x/S2x Microcontroller (MCU) family - further extending its performance efficient LPC5500 MCU series with the second of seven families planned for the series. The LPC552x/S2x MCU family offers significant advantages for developers, including pin-, software- and peripheral-compatibility to accelerate time to market, while leveraging 40-nm NVM process technology to deliver a cost- and power-efficient microcontroller platform. The LPC552x/S2x is a mainstream family in LPC5500 series, providing a perfect balance between security, performance efficiency and system integration for general embedded and industrial IoT markets. It combines the high-performance efficiency of the Cortex-M33 core with multiple high-speed interfaces, an integrated power management IC, and rich analog integration. Key features include: Cortex-M33 up to 150 MHz, FPU and MPU, From 256KB to 512 KB on-chip flash, and up to 256KB SRAM, Advanced security: PRINCE module for real-time encryption, CASPER for hardware acceleration, AES-256, SHA2 module, SRAM PUF (LPC55S2x only), FlexComm, USB HS, USB FS, 16-bit ADC with 5 differential channel pairs (or 10 singled-ended channels), ACMP, temperature sensor, 5 x 32b Timers, SCTimer/PWM, RTC, MRT, WWDT, Programmable Logic Unit, Power-saving modes, 1.8V to 3.6V, Operating temperature range -40 -degreeC to +105 –degreeC, Available in HLQFP100, VFBGA98 and HTQFP64 packages. Product Availability and Support: The LPC552x/S2x MCU family is available now from NXP and its distribution partners with a suggested resale price starting at $1.63 (USD) for 10,000-unit quantities. NXP will accompany the silicon release with a LPC55S28-based evaluation kit at a suggested resale price of $39 (USD). Third-party support is allowed from the broad Arm ecosystem. LPC55S6x MCU Family Increases Frequency and Expands Package Options. Launched earlier this year, the LPC55S6x MCU family increases its maximum core running frequency to 150MHz compared to the original 100MHz. In addition to the LQFP100 package, NXP now offers this device in BGA98 and LQFP64 (available Nov. 2019) packages for more design flexibility.'}{'symbol': 'PBCT', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "People's United Financial, Inc. (NasdaqGS:PBCT) completed the acquisition of United Financial Bancorp, Inc. (NasdaqGS:UBNK).", 'text': "People's United Financial, Inc. (NasdaqGS:PBCT) entered into an agreement to acquire United Financial Bancorp, Inc. (NasdaqGS:UBNK) for approximately $750 million on July 15, 2019. Under the terms of the agreement, United Financial Bancorp, Inc. shareholders will receive 0.875 shares of People's United Financial, Inc. (NasdaqGS:PBCT) stock for each share held. The transaction is valued at $14.74 per United Financial Bancorp, Inc. share, based on the closing price of People's United Financial, Inc.’s common stock on July 12, 2019. At the effective time, stock option of United Financial, whether or not then vested or free of conditions to payment, shall be cancelled and converted into the right to receive a number of shares of People's United common stock equal to the quotient of (i)\xa0the product of (A)\xa0the number of shares of United Financial common stock subject to such option,\xa0multiplied\xa0by (B)\xa0the excess, if any, of the per share stock consideration over the exercise price per share of such option,\xa0divided\xa0by People's United’s share closing price. Each performance-based restricted stock unit (PSU) of United Financial and each other outstanding equity-based award shall be cancelled and converted into the right to receive a number of shares of People's United common stock equal to the product of\xa0the number of shares of United Financial subject to such PSU or equity-based award, multiplied\xa0by the exchange ratio. Upon closing, People's United Financial, Inc. will hold 90% of the combined entity while United Financial Bancorp, Inc. will hold 10%. Following the merger, United Bank, a wholly owned subsidiary of United Financial, will merge with and into People’s United Bank, National Association, a wholly owned subsidiary of People’s United, with People’s United Bank, National Association surviving.\n\nThe merger agreement provides that a termination fee of $28.28 million will be payable by United Financial to People’s United upon termination of the agreement under certain circumstances. Completion of the transaction is subject to the receipt of regulatory approvals including the approval of the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency and the State of Connecticut Department of Banking, approval of shareholders of United Financial, authorization for listing on NASDAQ Global Select Market of the shares of People’s United to be issued in the merger, the effectiveness of the registration statement on Form\xa0S-4\xa0for the People’s United common stock to be issued in the merger, People's United and United Financial having received the written opinion from Simpson Thacher\xa0& Bartlett LLP and Sullivan\xa0& Cromwell LLP respectively, to the effect that the merger will be treated as a reorganization within the meaning of Section\xa0368(a) of the Code.\xa0The Board of Directors of United Financial received an opinion of Sandler O’Neill & Partners, LP to the effect that, the exchange ratio in the merger is fair from a financial point of view to the holders of common stock of United Financial. The transaction has been unanimously approved by Boards of Directors of People's United and United Financial. The Board of United Financial Bancorp, Inc. recommends shareholders to vote in favor of the transaction in a meeting expected on October\xa022, 2019. As of September 5, 2019, the registration statement became effective. As of October 11, 2019, all requisite regulatory approvals and waivers necessary to complete the merger were obtained.\n\nThe transaction is expected to close during the fourth quarter of 2019. As of October 11, 2019, consummation of the merger is expected to be effective on November\xa01, 2019. People's United Financial, Inc. expects the transaction to be $0.07 accretive to earnings per common share based on fully phased-in cost savings, with a tangible book value earn-back of approximately 2.3 years and an IRR of approximately 18%. Frank Cicero, Jordan Banov, Roger Wang, Dan Gerard and Jack Parkhurst\xa0of Keefe, Bruyette & Woods, Inc. acted as financial advisors and Lee Meyerson, Johanna Mayer, Lauren Kim, Adam Cohen, Spencer Sloan, Jeannine McSweeney, Jason Fixelle, Jonathan Goldstein and Sarah Katz of Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP acted as legal advisors for People's United Financial, Inc. Brian Sterling and Jon Doyle of Sandler O’Neill & Partners acted as financial advisors and fairness opinion provider and C. Andrew Gerlach, Marc Treviño, Eric Wang and Mehdi Ansari of Sullivan & Cromwell LLP acted as legal advisors for United Financial Bancorp, Inc. Frank Cicero, Jordan Banov, Roger Wang of Stifel Financial Corp. (NYSE:SF) acted as financial advisors to People's United. Morrow Sodali LLC acted as proxy solicitor for United Financial Bancorp, Inc. and will receive a fee of $15,000 for its services. RP Financial, LC acted as financial advisor for United Financial Bancorp, Inc. United Financial has agreed to pay Sandler O’Neill a transaction fee in an amount equal to 1.00% of the aggregate merger consideration, which transaction fee is contingent upon the closing of the merger. At the time of announcement of the merger, Sandler O’Neill’s transaction fee was approximately $7.5 million. Sandler O’Neill also received a $0.5 million fee upon rendering its fairness opinion to United Financial’s board of directors. Computershare, Inc. acted as the transfer agent and registrar to People’s United.\nPeople's United Financial, Inc. (NasdaqGS:PBCT) completed the acquisition of United Financial Bancorp, Inc. (NasdaqGS:UBNK) on November 1, 2019. The fair value of the consideration transferred in the United Financial acquisition totaled $723.6 million and consisted of 44.7 million shares of People’s United common stock.\n"}{'symbol': 'PNC', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The PNC Financial Services Group, Inc. Issues Inaugural Green Bond', 'text': "The PNC Financial Services Group, Inc. (PNC) announced the closing of its inaugural Green Bond issuance. The proceeds will fund eligible projects that promote a transition to a low-carbon economy and offer sustainability benefits across three categories aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, including renewable energy, energy efficiency and green buildings. PNC's Green Bond Framework supports the company's existing initiatives, and represents an opportunity to increase support for a future low-carbon economy. This offering was made only by means of a prospectus supplement and an accompanying prospectus filed as part of an effective shelf registration statement filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on Form S-3."}{'symbol': 'PTC', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'PTC Inc. (NasdaqGS:PTC) completed the acquisition of Onshape Inc.', 'text': 'PTC Inc. (NasdaqGS:PTC) signed a definitive agreement to acquire Onshape Inc. for approximately $470 million on October 23, 2019. The consideration is payable in cash. The base consideration of $470 million will involve deduction for debt payoff amount, aggregate amount of change in control payments and net working capital deficiency while excess cash as on the closing balance sheet will be added. The acquisition includes class A and B common shares, Series A, B, C and D preferred shares and in the money options. Each share of restricted stock outstanding shall be cancelled and converted into the right to receive cash equal to the repurchase price for such share, to be paid by Onshape, or PTC on Onshape’s behalf. An amount of $47 million will be deposited in escrow account as security for indemnification obligations. PTC expects to draw on its credit facility to fund the acquisition price. Onshape Inc. will operate as a business unit within PTC Inc., with current management reporting directly to PTC Inc.’s President and Chief Executive Officer, Jim Heppelmann. John McEleney, co-founder of Onshape Inc., will assume a senior role leading the Onshape business at PTC Inc. \n\nThe transaction is subject to regulatory approval, approval by shareholders of Onshape, no more than 3% of the outstanding shares of Onshape stock on an as-converted basis shall having exercised appraisal rights, entry into escrow agreement and paying agent agreement, resignation of directors and officers of Onshape, termination of certain rights and agreements, termination of options and equity plans of Onshape and the waiting period under the Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust law having expired and satisfaction of other closing conditions. The agreement has been unanimously approved by the Board of Directors Onshape. The Board of PTC has also approved the transaction. The transaction is expected to be completed in November 2019. Barclays acted as financial advisor to PTC Inc. while Matthew C. Dallett of Locke Lord LLP acted as legal advisor. Joseph J. Basile, Corey Brown, Brendan Burke, Jason Roche, Teresa Martland, Nicholas Romanos, Christopher Natkanski, Chasse Osborn and John D. Patterson of Foley Hoag LLP acted as legal advisors for Onshape.\nPTC Inc. (NasdaqGS:PTC) completed the acquisition of Onshape Inc. on November 1, 2019. Jon Hirschtick, President of Onshape, assumed a senior role leading the OnShape business at PTC and will reporting directly to Jim Heppelmann.\n'}{'symbol': 'QRVO', 'date': '2019-11-01 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Qorvo Posts Q2 EPS Of $1.52', 'text': "QORVO® ANNOUNCES FISCAL 2020 SECOND QUARTER FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.52.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.30 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ANNOUNCED TODAY AUTHORIZATION OF A NEW $1 BILLION SHARE REPURCHASE PROGRAM.SEES DECEMBER 2019 QUARTER REVENUE IN RANGE OF $840 MILLION TO $860 MILLION.SEES DECEMBER 2019 QUARTER NON-GAAP DILUTED EPS OF $1.67 AT MIDPOINT OF GUIDANCE.QTRLY GAAP REVENUE FOR QORVO'S $807 MILLION VERSUS $884.4 MILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.30, REVENUE VIEW $754.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.35, REVENUE VIEW $758.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. authorizes a Buyback Plan.', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. has authorized a buyback plan in November, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'RSG', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Massachusetts Teamsters on Strike at Republic Services Extend Picket Line to Georgia', 'text': "Sanitation workers on strike at Republic Services, Inc. in Marshfield, Mass., extended their picket line to Republic's operations in Cumming, Ga., early this morning. Republic Services workers in Cumming who are members of Teamsters Local 728 refused to cross the picket line in solidarity. Trash service for over 70,000 residents in the communities of Cumming and Alpharetta were affected by this action today. Trash pickup for businesses and construction sites in Milton, Johns Creek, Roswell, Canton and Woodstock are affected as well. The Massachusetts workers who are members of Teamsters Local 25 in Boston have been on strike since August 29 of this year. They are on an Unfair Labor Practice strike to protest Republic's violations of federal laws that protect workers' rights."}{'symbol': 'STX', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Seagate Technology Says Q1 Earnings Per Share $0.74', 'text': 'SEAGATE TECHNOLOGY REPORTS FISCAL FIRST QUARTER 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.03.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.74.Q1 REVENUE $2.58 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.57 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.01 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RAISED QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND TO $0.65 PER SHARE PAYABLE ON JANUARY 8, 2020.SEES REVENUE OF $2.72 BILLION, PLUS OR MINUS 5% IN Q2 .SEES NON-GAAP DILUTED EPS OF $1.32, PLUS OR MINUS 5% IN Q2 .'}{'symbol': 'STX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Seagate Technology plc Provides Earnings Guidance for Fiscal Second Quarter Ending December 2019; Provides Financial Guidance for the Fiscal 2020', 'text': 'Seagate Technology plc provided earnings guidance for its fiscal second quarter ending 2019. For the period, the company expects revenue of $2.72 billion, plus or minus 5%.The company continue to expect revenue and profitability to grow in fiscal 2020, with the second half projected to be somewhat stronger than the first, supported by its16-terabyte ramp and improving mass capacity storage demand.'}{'symbol': 'SEE', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Law Offices of Howard G. Files Securities Class Action on Behalf of Sealed Air Corporation Investors', 'text': 'Law Offices of Howard G. Smith announced that a class action lawsuit has been filed on behalf of investors who purchased Sealed Air Corporation common stock between November 5, 2014 and August 6, 2018, inclusive (the “Class Period”). Sealed Air investors have until January 2, 2020 to file a lead plaintiff motion. The complaint filed in this class action alleges that throughout the Class Period, Defendants made materially false and/or misleading statements, as well as failed to disclose material adverse facts about the Company’s business, operations, and prospects. Specifically, Defendants failed to disclose to investors: (1) that the Company had hired its auditor, E&Y, pursuant to a conflicted and improper process and in order to help facilitate defendants’ efforts to engage in accounting fraud; (2) that Sealed Air’s deduction of $1.49 billion, in connection with a settlement resolving asbestos-related liabilities, was indefensible and done for the improper purpose of artificially inflating the Company’s financial results; (3) that Sealed Air had artificially inflated its earnings, cash flows, and operating income; (4) that, as a result of the foregoing, the Company’s financial statements were materially false and misleading; and (5) that as a result, defendants’ statements about its business, operations, and prospects, were materially false and misleading and/or lacked a reasonable basis at all relevant times.'}{'symbol': 'SRE', 'date': '2019-11-01 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Oncor Reports Q3 Net Income $263 Million Versus $194 Million', 'text': 'ONCOR REPORTS STRONG Q3 2019 RESULTS.ONCOR ELECTRIC DELIVERY COMPANY LLC QTRLY OPERATING REVENUES $1,211 MILLION VERSUS $1,095 MILLION.ONCOR ELECTRIC DELIVERY COMPANY LLC QTRLY NET INCOME $263 MILLION VERSUS $194 MILLION.ONCOR ELECTRIC DELIVERY COMPANY LLC QTRLY TOTAL ELECTRIC ENERGY VOLUMES 40,834 GIGAWATT-HOURS VERSUS 38,163 GIGAWATT-HOURS.'}{'symbol': 'SRE', 'date': '2019-11-01 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sempra Energy Reports Q3 Adjusted Earnings Per Share $1.50', 'text': "REPORTS STRONG THIRD-QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.50.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.84.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.47 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.70 TO $7.50.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.00 TO $6.50.SEES FY 2020 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $12.78 TO $14.26.RAISES 2019 EPS GUIDANCE; ISSUES 2020 GAAP AND AFFIRMS 2020 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE.RECEIVES APPROVAL OF CALIFORNIA UTILITIES' SAFETY AND RELIABILITY-BASED GENERAL RATE CASE.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $2,758 MILLION VERSUS $2,565 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $2.94 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ON A GAAP BASIS, CO'S EARNINGS-PER-COMMON-SHARE (EPS) GUIDANCE RANGE FOR FULL-YEAR 2019 IS $6.50 TO $7.00.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.09 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $7.04 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}{'symbol': 'SRE', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sempra Energy Provides Earnings Guidance for the Full Years of 2019 and 2020; Announces Impairment Losses for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': "Sempra Energy provided earnings guidance for the full years of 2019 and 2020. On a GAAP basis, the company's earnings-per-common-share (EPS) guidance range for full-year 2019 is $6.50 to $7.00.The company also issued its full-year 2020 GAAP EPS guidance range of $12.78 to $14.26.The company announced impairment losses for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the quarter, the company reported impairment losses of $43 million compared to $4 million a year ago."}{'symbol': 'NOW', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ALIGM, ALIGM Annual Conference 2019, Nov 04, 2019', 'text': 'ALIGM, ALIGM Annual Conference 2019, Nov 04, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'TDY', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teledyne Technologies Incorporated and Teledyne Netherlands B.V., as Borrowers, Entered into an Amended and Restated Term Loan Credit Agreement', 'text': 'Teledyne and its subsidiary, Teledyne Netherlands B.V., as borrowers, entered into an Amended and Restated Term Loan Credit Agreement (the “Amended Term Loan Credit Agreement”) that amends and restates the Term Loan Credit Agreement dated as of March 17, 2017, by and among Teledyne and Teledyne Netherlands BV, as borrowers, the several banks and other financial institutions from time to time parties thereto as lenders, Bank of America, N.A., as administrative agent, and BofA Securities Inc., as sole book manager and sole lead arranger (the “Existing Term Loan Credit Agreement”). Pursuant to the Amended Term Loan Credit Agreement, the lenders thereunder made unsecured term loans in an aggregate principal amount of $150 million, denominated in US dollars, $100 million of which was used to repay outstanding loans under the Existing Term Loan Credit Agreement, which had a maturity date of October 30, 2019. Teledyne Brown Engineering Inc., Teledyne Instruments Inc., Teledyne Scientific & Imaging, LLC, Teledyne LeCroy Inc., Teledyne Defense Electronics, LLC and Teledyne Technologies International Corp., each of which is a subsidiary of Teledyne and a guarantor of the indebtedness under the Credit Agreement (as defined below) and certain other indebtedness of Teledyne, are also guarantors of the loans made under the Amended Term Loan Credit Agreement. Teledyne is also a guarantor for the loans made under the Amended Term Loan Credit Agreement to Teledyne Netherlands B.V.'}{'symbol': 'TFX', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Teleflex Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'TELEFLEX REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.97 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.85 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 REVENUE $648.3 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $643.5 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.75 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE UP 6 TO 6.5 PERCENT.LOWERED 2019 GUIDANCE RANGE FOR GAAP REVENUE GROWTH FROM A RANGE OF BETWEEN 6.0% AND 6.5% TO A RANGE OF BETWEEN 5.75% AND 6.0%.TELEFLEX - INCREASED 2019 GUIDANCE RANGE FOR CONSTANT CURRENCY REVENUE GROWTH FROM TO RANGE OF BETWEEN 8.0% AND 8.25%.INCREASED 2019 GUIDANCE RANGE FOR GAAP DILUTED EPS FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS FROM A RANGE OF BETWEEN $6.82 AND $6.94.NARROWED 2019 GUIDANCE RANGE FOR ADJUSTED DILUTED EPS FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS TO A RANGE OF BETWEEN $11.05 AND $11.10.INCREASE IN FULL YEAR 2019 GAAP DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE RANGE IS PRIMARILY DUE TO A DISCRETE TAX BENEFIT, RECOGNIZED IN Q3.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $11.02, REVENUE VIEW $2.60 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'VZ', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verizon Announces Results of Its Tender Offers for 11 Series of Notes', 'text': 'Verizon Communications Inc. announced the results of its previously announced 11 separate offers to purchase for cash any and all of the outstanding series of notes listed in the table below. Each offer to purchase a series of Notes is referred to as an Offer and collectively, as the Offers. The Offers were made upon the terms and subject to the conditions set out in the Offer to Purchase dated October 24, 2019 relating to the Notes and the accompanying notice of guaranteed delivery. The customary conditions to the Offers have been satisfied. The Maximum Total Consideration Condition has been satisfied with respect to series of Notes with Acceptance Priority Level of 7 and higher. The aggregate Total Consideration payable for the series of Notes with Acceptance Priority Level 8 is greater than $4,600,000,000. Therefore, the Maximum Total Consideration Condition has not been satisfied with respect to series of Notes with an Acceptance Priority Level of 8 and lower. However, Verizon has decided to waive the Maximum Total Consideration Condition with respect to the series of Notes with an Acceptance Priority Level of 8 and lower. Accordingly, all Notes validly tendered at or prior to the Expiration Date and not validly withdrawn at or prior to the Withdrawal Date (as defined in the Offer to Purchase) have been accepted for purchase. Payment of the required cash amounts for any Notes accepted will be made on November 5, 2019. In addition to the applicable Total Consideration, holders whose Notes are accepted for purchase will receive a cash payment equal to the accrued and unpaid interest on such Notes from and including the immediately preceding interest payment date for such Notes to, but excluding, the Settlement Date. The aggregate Total Consideration for each series of Notes is set out in the table above. Interest will cease to accrue on the applicable Settlement Date for all Notes accepted in the Offers, including those tendered through the guaranteed delivery procedures.'}{'symbol': 'WU', 'date': '2019-11-01 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Western Union Reports Q3 GAAP Earnings Per Share Of $0.32', 'text': 'WESTERN UNION REPORTS THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.49.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.32.Q3 REVENUE $1.3 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.31 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.46 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AFFIRMS FULL-YEAR FINANCIAL OUTLOOK AND THREE-YEAR TARGETS.CONTINUES IMPLEMENTATION OF NEW GLOBAL STRATEGY TO DRIVE LONG-TERM GROWTH.STRENGTHENING OF DOLLAR AGAINST ARGENTINE PESO NEGATIVELY IMPACTED REPORTED REVENUE BY 2% IN QUARTER.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.76, REVENUE VIEW $5.32 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'WHR', 'date': '2019-11-01 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Whirlpool Corp Says Will Continue Production At Naples Manufacturing Plant In Near-Term', 'text': "WHIRLPOOL CORP - WILL CONTINUE PRODUCTION AT NAPLES MANUFACTURING PLANT IN NEAR-TERM.WHIRLPOOL CORP - PRELIMINARY AGREEMENT TO SELL NAPLES PLANT TO A THIRD-PARTY PURCHASER REMAINS IN PLACE, SUBJECT TO FURTHER NEGOTIATIONS.WHIRLPOOL CORP -  WILL RESUME NEGOTIATIONS WITH UNIONS AND ITALIAN GOVERNMENT RELATED TO COMPANY'S EXIT OF NAPLES MANUFACTURING PLANT.WHIRLPOOL CORP - INTENDS TO COMPLETE ITS RESTRUCTURING AND CEASE PRODUCTION AT NAPLES PLANT IN COMING MONTHS WITH EXIT EXPECTED IN 2020.WHIRLPOOL - LIKELY TRENDING TOWARD UPPER END OF ITS GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE GUIDANCE RANGE..WHIRLPOOL - NOW ESTIMATES ABOUT $40 - $50 MILLION OF $127 MILLION TOTAL COSTS WILL BE INCURRED IN 2019 AND REMAINDER WILL OCCUR IN 2020."}{'symbol': 'WLTW', 'date': '2019-11-01 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Willis Towers Watson Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $0.58', 'text': 'WILLIS TOWERS WATSON REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.31.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.58.Q3 REVENUE ROSE 7 PERCENT TO $1.99 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.31 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY TOTAL ORGANIC REVENUE GROWTH OF 6%.WILLIS TOWERS WATSON - EXPECT FOREIGN CURRENCY TRANSLATION TO BE AROUND A $0.04 HEADWIND TO ADJUSTED DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE FOR REMAINDER OF 2019.CONTINUE TO SEE A MODEST IMPROVEMENT WITH PRICING IN MARKET.THERE ARE STILL SIGNIFICANT UNCERTAINTIES WITH RESPECT TO BREXIT.BELIEVE COMPANY IS WELL POSITIONED TO OPERATE IN A POST-BREXIT ENVIRONMENT.'}{'symbol': 'XLNX', 'date': '2019-11-01 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Xilinx Alveo Accelerators Power SK Telecom's Real-Time AI-based Physical Intrusion and Theft Detection Service", 'text': "Xilinx, Inc. and SK Telecom announced that SK Telecom has adopted Xilinx®Alveo Datacenter Accelerator cards to power a real-time AI-based physical intrusion and theft detection service. SK Telecom's AI inference accelerator (AIX) implemented on Xilinx Alveo cards provides efficient and accurate physical intrusion detection using deep neural networks. ADT CAPS CO., LTD., South Korea's second largest physical security company, licenses and commercially deploys the physical intrusion detection service. SK Telecom's AI-based physical intrusion detection service, T viewTM, monitors hundreds of thousands of customers' commercial and home camera systems in real-time and dispatches security guards under physical intrusion circumstances. Processing a large volume of data from thousands of cameras using deep neural networks necessitates a powerful AI accelerator that can provide enough throughput and accuracy. T view uses SK Telecom's AI inference accelerator (AIX), implemented on Xilinx Alveo U250 cards. Running on servers in SK Telecom's data center, Alveo U250 cards have demonstrated high throughput and accuracy in theft detection services. The cards deliver lower detection latency and have achieved superior throughput (frames per second) compared to leading GPUs and have proven to be more cost effective. The improved throughput and accuracy delivered by Alveo cards means more customers will have access to real-time, AI-based security services, and a more reliable protection against security threats. Xilinx Alveo accelerator cards are designed to meet the performance and flexibility needs of data center AI workloads, providing 10X higher performance1 for AI-based speech translation and over 3X higher throughout for video analytics pipelines compared to GPUs. Built on the Xilinx® 16nm UltraScale+™ architecture, Alveo accelerators are adaptable to changing algorithms and acceleration requirements, enabling domain specific architectures that optimize performance for a range of workloads without changing hardware, and while reducing overall cost of ownership. The commercial deployment of Xilinx Alveo cards in SK Telecom's data center for AI services builds upon the announcement and success of SK Telecom's automated speech-recognition (ASR) application powered by Xilinx FPGAs to accelerate NUGU, a voice-activated assistant. SK Telecom's AIX accelerator, implemented on the Alveo U250, and the T view service are currently available in South Korea and are expected to be available globally in fall 2020. The T view is also expected to be commercially available as a rebranded solution from other SK Telecom licensed companies."}